From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-2f: run the SD card at 50 MHz

In UHS SDR104 mode at 150 MHz every read from the SD card fails, so the
kernel finds no partitions and cannot mount the root file system. Use
high speed at 50 MHz, as the mainline kernels do.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
diff --color -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts	2026-10-23 08:59:38.499682216 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts	2026-10-23 08:59:38.509824399 +0200
@@ -396,15 +396,12 @@
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	disable-wp;
-	max-frequency = <150000000>;
+	/* UHS SDR104 at 150 MHz fails every read: use high speed at 50 MHz */
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdmmc_clk &sdmmc_cmd &sdmmc_det &sdmmc_bus4>;
 	rockchip,default-sample-phase = <90>;
 	supports-sd;
-	sd-uhs-sdr12;
-	sd-uhs-sdr25;
-	sd-uhs-sdr50;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vccio_sd>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_sd>;
 	status = "okay";
